WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.335
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:05.905
Now I'm sure everyone here
is familiar with the McRib,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:09.175
the sandwich from McDonald's
with an almost cult-like status,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.611
that shows up out of the blue
and sticks around

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.813
for a couple of months or so
before disappearing again.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:18.518
Well, for the past 30 years,
comedy writers have been writing

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.753
about the McRib
every single time it comes back,

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:25.758
each time, each comedy writer,
acting like they were the first

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.495
to observe the strangeness
of a seasonal sandwich.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.995
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:32.832
Well, one of my writers came to
me with a McRib idea and said,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.333
"I think I have a fresh take."

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.369
And I said, "I doubt that."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:40.306
"But let's hear it."
And then he told me.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.877
And I think he actually
did find a fresh take.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:47.380
Well, here he is,
my writer Ben Warheit.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.515
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:54.387 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.523
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.992
-Hi, McRib.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.461
It's me, your son.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.895
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.430 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.533
I heard you might be
coming back soon.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.336
Listen, I -- I don't want
to fight with you.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.540
I just want to say,
you can't keep

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.508
walking into and out
of our lives anymore.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.909
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:20.546
Showing up unannounced,
"Hey, everybody, surprise!

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.815
The McRib is back!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.751
Yeah, surprise.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.987
You know, there was a time
I would have given anything

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.722
just to be near you?

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.857
I'd skip school,
blow off my friends,

00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:34.393
I'd come looking for you.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.762
You'd already be gone.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.163
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.666
And I don't even know when
you're planning to come back.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:42.969
I mean, sure, the Shamrock Shake
leaves his kids all the time.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.269
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:45.438
But at least they know

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.740
when his bright-green ass
is gonna come home.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.041
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.843
-Right? I mean, we've never
seen this take before.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.678
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:57.550
I gotta say...

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.186
I think the acting is,
uh, pretty good, too.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.787
Let's -- Let's go back.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.256 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.758
-You know what, McRib?
I'm grown.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.793
I can deal with it.

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:13.098
But Emma, your daughter,
you missed her prom.

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:15.668
And mom...

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:19.339
she can't even show her face
at a Fourth of July barbecue.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.073
But you don't care, do you?

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:23.676
No, 'cause you only do
what you wanna do,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.778
show up in town,
out of the blue.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.046
Make a quick buck,
and spend time with people

00:02:28.046 --> 00:02:29.248
who, let's be honest,

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.250
they're not your friends,
they're [bleep] fans.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.584
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:35.454
They're just gonna chew you up
and [bleep] you out --

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.790
quickly!
Faster than most foods.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.824
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.326 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.895
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:46.632
You know what you are?
You -- You're sad.

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.702
You're a sad old man
just chasing your glory days.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.537
You don't love your family,
because how can you

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:54.440
love anything
when you don't love yourself?

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.609
So, next time you think you just
want to drop in unannounced,

00:02:57.609 --> 00:03:00.579
do us all a big favor --
stay away.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:02.615
'Cause we don't want you here.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.716
And if you think for a second --

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.017
-Uh, Ben, I'm sorry.
Wait.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:08.821
I'm -- I'm getting a message
from the McRib right now.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.523
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.557
-Yeah?

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.025
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.595
-He says he's coming back.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.665
-Papa's coming home!
Whoo-hoo!

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.100
Oh, I -- I gotta go
to the balloon store!

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.001
Band -- Band,
play some fanfare!

00:03:23.001 --> 00:03:24.070
Play some good music!

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.071 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.439
I gotta go!
Bye!

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.142 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:34.180
-Now, I told you that was
a fresh take, and I --

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.481
I stand by that.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.849
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.485
I didn't say "good take."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.088
But we takes
the takes we can get.

